From a7c9aa5687aa8d735f558c1dae8ee3319483239f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 18:09:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Give the fullscreen hero text room to clear the fixed header
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured live on silvagnidario.com at a common desktop viewport
(1920x889): the eyebrow ("Visual creator - Bologna, Italia") sat at
y=85 while the fixed glass header's bottom edge was at y=106 — the
text was rendering ~20px *behind* the header, not below it, because
`items-center` centers this block on the viewport's own height, and a
three-line heading is tall enough to push its top past the header
whenever the viewport isn't especially tall.

Adds `pt-128` to the centred text wrapper. Centering only gives back
half of whatever padding-top adds to the block's height, so this
reads as roughly +64px more clearance above the eyebrow — enough to
clear the header with room to spare — without switching the variant
away from being vertically centred over its background, which is the
one thing that wasn't broken here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015hHvGTWvAaz9WDpZm7oPPi
---
 src/components/blocks/hero.tsx | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/components/blocks/hero.tsx b/src/components/blocks/hero.tsx
index c0a1d60..e0aae09 100644
--- a/src/components/blocks/hero.tsx
+++ b/src/components/blocks/hero.tsx
@@ -89,7 +89,19 @@ export function Hero({ block }: { block: HeroBlock }) {
           {/* Overlay scuro per garantire contrasto al testo sopra il video */}
           <div className="absolute inset-0 bg-surface-inverse/40" />
         </div>
-        <div className="page-grid relative z-10 w-full text-ink-inverse [&_.text-ink-2]:text-ink-inverse/80 [&_.text-ink-muted]:text-ink-inverse/70">
+        {/*
+         * `items-center` on the section balances this block around the
+         * viewport's own centre, so how much air sits above the eyebrow
+         * depends on how tall the heading happens to be — on a three-line
+         * heading at a typical desktop viewport height it measured out
+         * negative: the eyebrow sat ~20px *behind* the fixed glass header,
+         * not below it. `pt-128` here nudges the whole centred block down
+         * (centering only gives back half of what padding-top adds, so this
+         * reads as roughly +64px of clearance) without pinning it to the
+         * top the way the typographic variant's section padding does — this
+         * variant is meant to stay visually centred over its background.
+         */}
+        <div className="page-grid relative z-10 w-full pt-128 text-ink-inverse [&_.text-ink-2]:text-ink-inverse/80 [&_.text-ink-muted]:text-ink-inverse/70">
           {text}
         </div>
       </section>
